-- title:
--   Cartier pairing is perfect on K-points, K algebraically closed of characteristic 0
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime, $h$ a natural number, and let $G, G'$ be $p$-divisible groups of height $h$ over $R$ in the sense of the structure [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199): each consists of commutative Hopf $R$-algebras $G.level\ v$ that are finite free of rank $p^{vh}$ with cocommutative comultiplication, together with surjective bialgebra transition maps $G.level\,(v+1) \to G.level\ v$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal under the $p^v$-fold convolution power of the identity. Let $D$ be a Cartier duality datum between $G$ and $G'$, i.e. coalgebra-algebra isomorphisms $G'.level\ v \cong \mathrm{CartierDual}\ R\ (G.level\ v)$ compatible with the transitions up to multiplication by $p$. Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero which is an $R$-algebra, and fix $v$. Points are $R$-algebra homomorphisms into $K$, a group under convolution, and for $f \in G.Point\ K\ v$, $\psi \in G'.Point\ K\ v$ the pairing is $\sum_i f(b_i)\,\psi(\theta^{-1}(b^i))$, where $(b_i)$ is the chosen $R$-basis of $G.level\ v$, $(b^i)$ its coordinate functionals and $\theta$ the linear isomorphism $G'.level\ v \cong \mathrm{Dual}_R(G.level\ v)$ induced by $D$. The conclusion is the conjunction of four assertions: if $\langle f,\psi\rangle = 1$ for all $\psi$ then $f = 1$; if $\langle f,\psi\rangle = 1$ for all $f$ then $\psi = 1$; every monoid homomorphism $\chi : G'.Point\ K\ v \to K^\times$ equals $\psi \mapsto \langle f,\psi\rangle$ for some $f$; and every monoid homomorphism $\chi : G.Point\ K\ v \to K^\times$ equals $f \mapsto \langle f,\psi\rangle$ for some $\psi$.
--
--   This is the perfectness of the Cartier pairing at each finite level on points with values in an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero: the two point groups are mutually dual finite abelian groups. It is used in the study of the Tate module of a Cartier-dual pair of $p$-divisible groups, in particular by the results identifying elements annihilated by the pairing and the divisibility statements at level $v$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_CartierDuality_eq_one_of_forall_pair_eq_one_and_exists_pair_eq_of_isAlgClosed.lean

